s still separate.\n\nVerification and custody also differ. CLI tagged enrolment requires filesystem custody (invitations.ts:443), verifies exact original bytes (521), member/key/controller facts (558), the bound Directory and sibling incarnations (90), and inbox genesis/owner (211,576). Page uses its retained nonextractable browser signer (join-custody.ts:141), exact receipt (data.ts:380), then Directory/Membership and caller standing (data.ts:398, main.ts:900); that path verifies no inbox. CLI person join verifies its accepted signed entry and waits for the derived inbox to activate (commands.ts:639). MCP uses its configured server signer, verifies the kept signed entry and derives an inbox seed (service.ts:1505,1523), then writes configuration before its separately advised inbox wait. It does not run the tagged CLI Directory/inbox judge. Page normalizes trailing slashes for service admission at data.ts:306; MCP compares service strings directly at service.ts:1497.\n\nThe item 1 report precedes any join source edit. The shared parser/judge build, documentation and parity witnesses remain phase 3 after C1 and M1a. Hosted MCP stays closed; this report closes no implementation or live acceptance.","body":{"implementation":"Items 2 and 3 remain phase 3 after C1 and M1a.","phase":"read-only inventory","to":"planner"}}